      "playwright": "Most of this page is plain DOM, so role and testid locators did the work; the harder parts were proving the analysis is correct rather than just rendered. For focus order the browser is the oracle: one keyboard.press('Tab') on a fresh page, then toBeFocused on the positive-tabindex button — it has to happen before any click, because Chrome continues Tab navigation from the last clicked point. The SVG colour filters cannot be asserted meaningfully through pixels in a stable way, so the spec checks the applied computed filter with toHaveCSS and that each filter primitive exists, and the actual visual effect was reviewed by screenshot. Screenshot comparisons were not used; exact contrast ratios are a far more precise oracle than a pixel diff.",
