      "risks": [
        "Font rendering differing between the two canvases if they were ever drawn at different times with a web font still loading (avoided by using system fonts only).",
        "Pointer-to-canvas coordinate mapping breaking when the canvas is scaled by CSS at narrow widths, putting masks in the wrong place.",
        "Region grouping merging adjacent regressions (padding and colour both touch the button) so region counts shift if the layout moves."
      ],
      "playwright": "The page is itself a screenshot comparator, so the spec deliberately does not use toHaveScreenshot: the oracle is the comparator's numeric output (diff pixels, allowed, regions) exposed as DOM text. The first probing run found that the initial colour drift was invisible even at threshold 0.05, which led to retuning it so the threshold test is meaningful. Mask drawing uses page.mouse down/move/up with steps, which also works on the Pixel 7 project because Chromium still dispatches pointer events for mouse input with touch emulation on. Test images are generated inside the page with a canvas and passed to setInputFiles as buffers, so no fixture files are needed.",
