      "playwright": "The page animates continuously, so the determinism tests install page.clock and pause it before navigation. That stops requestAnimationFrame, and the spec drives the light simulation through window.__marfa.step() in exact increments. The star rotation is checked with geometry rather than pixels: the page exposes star() and polaris() screen positions for any time, and the spec compares angles and radii. Pixels are read only where the answer is certain (pure black outside the binocular eyepieces). The time-lapse is tested with clock.runFor, which advances the fake rAF clock. Web Audio can't be listened to in a headless browser, so the spec checks that no context exists before the gesture and that one exists after.",
