      "playwright": "A quilt is ideal for invariant testing because the geometry is exact. Coverage and fabric-share assertions run against polygon areas exposed by window.__quilt, which catches a wrong triangle far more reliably than a screenshot would. Clicking specific blocks on a scaled canvas is the hard part; the page reports each block's centre in CSS pixels, so the spec uses locator.click({ position }), which works with mouse on desktop and with touch emulation on Pixel 7. Pixel output is checked only through a sampled checksum that must change when quilting or fabrics change, so there are no brittle toHaveScreenshot baselines across font and GPU differences. The export test waits for the download event and checks the PNG magic bytes and the filename.",
