      "playwright": "The page exposes __emb with the words, the current vectors, the PCA result and the state, and the spec treats the vectors as input data only: every number it asserts on is recomputed in Node, including a full Jacobi eigen-decomposition to check the page's power iteration. Points carry data-pc1/data-pc2 attributes, so the SVG is verified through its coordinates, not pixels. One test measures point positions with getBoundingClientRect in page.evaluate and clicks an isolated one, which keeps the tap unambiguous on the Pixel 7 project; that is a little indirect, but it was chosen up front because labels and hit areas overlap in the clusters, so a hard-coded word could be covered by a neighbour after any change to the vectors. There is no randomness or timing on this page, so page.clock and seeds are not needed.",
