      "playwright": "page.clock does most of the work here. Installing it before navigation fakes performance.now, setInterval and requestAnimationFrame together, so runFor(2000) drives the 25 ms scheduler tick, the lookahead window and the playhead animation in lockstep and the log comes out identical every run. That only works on the silent path, which is why the page falls back to performance.now: the real AudioContext clock is not something page.clock can move, so the one real-audio test polls with expect.poll and checks relative gaps rather than absolute times. addInitScript made the missing and permanently suspended audio cases easy to set up. Range inputs are set through evaluate plus an input event, because fill() doesn't work on type=range. Everything passed on the first run, so this spec has not caught a regression yet.",
