      "playwright": "The page has no timers or randomness, so the spec needs no page.clock or seed. Its value is in the state logic. window.__supper exposes derived seat counts and the waitlist so the test's own model can be compared after every step, while user-facing assertions go through the real form, buttons and getByRole names such as 'Cancel reservation SSC-DEC-002 for Small Table'. page.setViewportSize made the two-layout check possible inside one test on both projects, though it tests the layout at two fixed widths rather than on real devices. keyboard.press drove the accordion; Space on a focused native button works the same on the Pixel 7 emulation. There are no screenshot assertions, so small visual regressions in the editorial styling would go unnoticed.",
